# No LAN IP belongs in this file. In local dev leave the two URLs UNSET: the app
# reads the Expo dev server's host at runtime (src/lib/config.ts) and pairs it
# with port 5001 for the API and 54321 for Supabase, so a new Wi-Fi address
# needs no edit here.
#
# Set them ONLY for production/staging or to force a specific host. Both are
# then used verbatim.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.yahora.example
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project>.supabase.co

# Backend port paired with the auto-detected dev host. Defaults to 5001, and
# must match backend/.env PORT.
#
# NOT 5000: on macOS the AirPlay Receiver (Control Center) binds port 5000 from
# boot and answers every request with a bodiless 403 Forbidden. Because that is
# a real HTTP response and not a connection failure, the app reports it as an
# application error — the login screen blames the university, the demo button
# says "Request failed (403)" — and nothing points at the port.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_PORT=5001

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<local anon key>

# Cloudflare Turnstile SITE key for the OTP login widget (TurnstileWebView).
# PUBLIC by design — it only identifies the widget. The SECRET key lives in the
# Supabase dashboard and must never appear in this repo, in this file or any
# other. Must be EXPO_PUBLIC_-prefixed: Expo inlines nothing else, so a
# VITE_-prefixed copy of the web's variable is invisible to the app.
# Without it the Send Code button stays disabled and the screen says why.
# For local dev against a Supabase with captcha off, Cloudflare's documented
# always-pass test key 1x00000000000000000000AA works on any hostname.
EXPO_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=<turnstile site key>